      "inspiredBy": "Japan",
      "source": "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/411AC0000000127",
      "sourceNote": "Japan's Act on National Flag and Anthem specifies a white field and a centered crimson disc, with the flag's 2:3 proportions and disc diameter of three-fifths the flag height. This original, optional ball panel treatment uses those colors and a centered disc; it does not reproduce the flag artwork, use rays, or infer a cosmetic from player nationality."
    },
    {
      "id": "tricolore",
      "name": "Tricolore Panels · France-inspired",
      "inspiredBy": "France",
      "source": "https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/codes/article_lc/LEGIARTI000006527453/2026-02-06",
      "sourceNote": "Article 2 of France's Constitution identifies the national emblem as the blue, white, and red tricolour. This original optional ball treatment applies those three colors to curved football panels, not a flag image or exact flag layout; it is player-selected and never inferred from nationality."
    },
    {
      "id": "auriverde",
      "name": "Auriverde Panels · Brazil-inspired",
      "inspiredBy": "Brazil",
      "source": "https://www.gov.br/planalto/pt-br/conheca-a-presidencia/biblioteca-da-pr/simbolos-nacionais/bandeira/bandeira-nacional",
      "sourceNote": "The Brazilian Presidency describes the national flag's green field, yellow diamond, blue celestial sphere and white band. This original optional ball pattern uses those colors and broad shapes without the stars or motto; it is player-selected and never inferred from nationality."
    }
